## Qt 6

The window links to Qt 6 (Widgets, Gui, Core) at runtime. Open-source Qt is
available under the GNU LGPL version 3 and under the GNU GPL. The Qt used to
build StopWatch keeps the license of that installation.

Qt source and its license texts are in the Qt directory from the build, and at:

https://download.qt.io
https://www.qt.io/licensing/open-source-lgpl-obligations
https://www.gnu.org/licenses/lgpl-3.0.html
https://doc.qt.io/qt-6/licenses-used-in-qt.html

The last page lists what Qt itself bundles (BSD, MIT, and others).
The Qt libraries can be replaced with a compatible build.
The program says the same under Help, About StopWatch and About Qt.

## Catch2

Tests may download Catch2 v3.5.2 from https://github.com/catchorg/Catch2
(Boost Software License 1.0). It is not linked into StopWatch or StopWatch-gui.

## Sounds

The timer plays freedesktop theme files through paplay or pw-play when they
are installed. Those files belong to the system. Otherwise the program plays
a short tone of its own.
